<title>JAPAN: Nippon Meat down on embezzlement announcement.</title>
<headline>Nippon Meat down on embezzlement announcement.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Nippon Meat Packers Inc fell sharply on the Tokyo Stock Exchange on Monday morning due to a company announcement on the weekend about suspected embezzlement by an official at its U.S. unit, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0049 GMT Nippon Meat shares were down 60 yen at 1,320 yen.  </p>
<p>The large Japanese meat packing firm said on Saturday that an official at its wholly owned U.S. subsidiary was suspected of embezzling between $80 million and $100 million.</p>
<p>Company president Hiroji Ohkoso told a news conference that it was an isolated incident and that nobody else in the company was involved. He added that it would not result in any significant loss for the company.</p>
</text>
